## 3. Levels

| Effective type                          | Level    | Gates                                                    | Reviewer               |
| --------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| `feat`, `refactor`, `breaking: true`    | **full** | all                                                      | yes, at activity close |
| `fix`, `perf`, `test`                   | medium   | changed format/lint + affected type + targeted tests     | no                     |
| `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `ci`, `build` | light    | changed format/lint + structure/docs + harness self-test | no                     |
| `verification: "none"`                  | none     | every gate skipped (explicit override only)              | no                     |

`task.type` is optional. The fallback is
`task.type ?? activity.type ?? 'medium'`. Unknown types default to **medium**,
not light: a false green is worse than a false red.

---

## 4. Commands

| Command                                             | Behaviour                               |
| --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs`                          | full (final gate)                       |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs --for-task <a>.<t>`       | level of that task                      |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs --explain <a>.<t>`        | level + gate set, no gates              |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs --fast`                   | changed-file iteration                  |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs --changed`                | auto light/medium from the working tree |
| `node scripts/harness.mjs --dev-build --skip-tests` | fast artifact/CSS check                 |
| `node --test scripts/harness-lib.spec.mjs`          | harness logic tests                     |

`--for-task` wins over `--fast`/`--changed`. `--skip-format`, `--skip-lint`,
`--skip-type`, `--skip-build`, `--skip-tests`, `--skip-contract` are escapes.
Running full with reduced gates is not a complete full verification. There is
no `--no-cache` until a cache exists.

---

## 5. Docs and tests per type

| Type                 | Tests                                        | Docs                                        | New components/services          |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `feat`               | new or extended spec                         | yes if public API, view or visible behavior | yes, with the project's file set |
| `fix` (not breaking) | regression test that fails without the fix   | only if the doc was wrong                   | no                               |
| `fix!` / `feat!`     | update affected specs                        | yes — docs described the old behavior       | update only                      |
| `refactor`           | if a contract changed; not for a pure rename | only if comments/README became stale        | no                               |
| `perf`               | behavior test or benchmark                   | no                                          | no                               |
| `test`               | yes (that is the task)                       | no                                          | no                               |
| `chore`              | no                                           | no                                          | no                               |
| `docs`               | no                                           | yes                                         | no                               |
| `style`              | no                                           | no                                          | no                               |
| `ci` / `build`       | no                                           | maybe the development workflow doc          | no                               |

